1️⃣ Concept

Each user/client has a token bucket stored in Redis.

Redis atomic operations (like INCR, EXPIRE, or Lua scripts) ensure thread-safe token updates across servers.

Requests consume tokens, and if no tokens are left, the request is rejected.

Key Advantages:

Works in distributed environments

Handles bursts

Scales horizontally

